# issue: none
# notes: An exact `bm25` `Score` declares a switch: its one-pass side keeps a match table
# notes: (per matching document its identity, token count and one entry per matched term)
# notes: and scores every match in its corpus pass; when that table would pass a quarter of
# notes: the plan's memory limit, the `two_pass` fallback keeps the corpus statistics alone
# notes: and scores each population row from its own text, read again by identity. Eighty
# notes: documents, each matching thirty of sixty query terms, hold about 180 KB of table: at the
# notes: default pool the read runs `one_pass`, at a 512 KiB pool `two_pass`, with the same
# notes: rows, the same order and the same F64 scores (contract E5: a read the engine answered
# notes: before keeps its answer when a faster mechanism lands). The plan claims and the
# notes: pool setting are engine-only.

--- runner
timeout_ms: 10000
environments:
  - target: omnigraph-engine
    storage: local-filesystem

--- schema
node Doc {
    slug: String @key
    text: String @index(fulltext, analyzer = "standard_v1")
}

